WEBVTT

00:04:29.469 --> 00:04:31.692
I had hundreds of emails.

00:04:31.716 --> 00:04:33.279
They were from people who said,

00:04:33.303 --> 00:04:36.251
"Thank you for finally giving
these women a voice."

00:04:36.275 --> 00:04:39.163
They were from readers who said,

00:04:39.187 --> 00:04:42.050
"I cried on my way to work,
reading these stories,

00:04:42.074 --> 00:04:44.441
because I felt seen for the first time."

00:04:45.116 --> 00:04:47.355
And they were from colleagues
of mine, who said,

00:04:47.379 --> 00:04:49.041
"I never thought a woman of color

00:04:49.065 --> 00:04:51.283
would be allowed to achieve
something like this

00:04:51.307 --> 00:04:52.841
at the 'New York Times.'"

00:04:53.878 --> 00:04:56.989
I also got about 4,000 reader submissions

00:04:57.013 --> 00:04:59.449
suggesting who else
we might have overlooked.

00:04:59.473 --> 00:05:02.547
And some of those are my favorite
stories in the project.